{"metadata":{"title":"Concurrent Order Selection with AutoARIMA","roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","modules":[{"name":"SwiftForecast"}]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Automated Time Series","anchor":"Automated-Time-Series","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMA","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAOrder","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMACriterion"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAParallel","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides & Tutorials","anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ArimaAndSarima","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SmoothingAndDecomposition","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/KoopmanOperator"],"generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Manually diagnosing autocorrelation functions (ACF) and partial autocorrelation functions (PACF) to select ARIMA orders is time-consuming and error-prone. Standard automated packages like R’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forecast::auto.arima"},{"text":" or Python’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pmdarima"},{"text":" search across candidate orders sequentially.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AutoARIMA"},{"type":"text","text":" evaluates the entire hyperparameter lattice simultaneously across all CPU cores on Apple Silicon using structured Swift Concurrency ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withThrowingTaskGroup"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"anchor":"Grid-Search-Architecture","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Grid Search Architecture"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["           Observed Time Series [y_1, y_2, ..., y_N]","                               │","       ┌───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┐","       ▼                       ▼                       ▼","ARIMA(1, 1, 0)          ARIMA(2, 1, 1)          ARIMA(0, 1, 2)","Task 1                  Task 2                  Task 3","   │                       │                       │","   ├─ Hannan-Rissanen      ├─ Hannan-Rissanen      ├─ Hannan-Rissanen","   └─ Compute AIC\/BIC      └─ Compute AIC\/BIC      └─ Compute AIC\/BIC","       │                       │                       │","       └───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┘","                               ▼","                withThrowingTaskGroup Collector","                               │","                               ▼","                 Sorted Leaderboard & Best Model"]},{"anchor":"Information-Criteria","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Information Criteria"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"AIC (Akaike Information Criterion)"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Penalizes model complexity while rewarding likelihood:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"$$\\text{AIC} = 2k - 2\\ln(L)$$"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"BIC (Bayesian Information Criterion)"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Imposes a stronger penalty proportional to sample size:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"$$\\text{BIC} = k\\ln(N) - 2\\ln(L)$$"}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Example-Usage","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Example Usage"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftForecast","","\/\/ 1. Initialize AutoARIMA with bounded search ranges","let autoArima = AutoARIMA(","    maxP: 3,","    maxD: 2,","    maxQ: 3,","    criterion: .aic",")","","\/\/ 2. Concurrently fit candidates across all cores","let result = try await autoArima.fit(series: historicalPrices)","print(\"Optimal Order: \\(autoArima.bestOrder!) with AIC: \\(autoArima.bestScore!)\")","","\/\/ 3. Generate multi-step forecasts","let forecast = try await autoArima.forecast(horizon: 12)","print(\"Forecasted points: \\(forecast.forecast.predictions)\")"]},{"anchor":"Stability--Convergence-Guarantees","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Stability & Convergence Guarantees"},{"anchor":"Zero-Variance-Degenerate-Inputs","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Zero-Variance Degenerate Inputs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If an input series is constant or exhibits zero numerical variance ($\\text{var} < 10^{-12}$), standard likelihood optimization can diverge or enter infinite loops. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AutoARIMA"},{"text":" detects zero variance upfront, immediately fitting an exact ARIMA(0, 0, 0) constant model:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Avoids matrix singularities in the Hannan-Rissanen and Yule-Walker algorithms."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Guarantees instant return without stalling the task group."}]}]}]},{"text":"Fixed Iteration Bound","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Fixed-Iteration-Bound"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All internal parameter search loops are strictly bounded by a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations = 500"},{"type":"text","text":" ceiling, ensuring that optimization cannot exceed the configured iteration bound in deterministic time across parallel worker threads."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Discover optimal autoregressive, integrated, and moving average orders across ((p, d, q) \\times (P, D, Q)_s) grids using parallel Swift Concurrency.","type":"t